<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/14298b10a2ce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Patriot missile: friend or foe?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1449a5ba353b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "More specifically, the Ministry of Defence Military Aircraft Accident Summary (PDF) notes that:" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1765a4f0f23c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This dynamic played out in the other fatal friendly fire incident involving a Patriot missile battery during the Iraq War, when a U.S. Navy F/A-18 aircraft was misidentified as a ballistic missile and shot down, killing the pilot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/20fe4d0ce0b4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The split-second decision led to one of the tragedies of the Iraq war last year: the dot was an RAF Tornado GR4, flown by Flight Lieutenants Kevin Main and David Williams who died instantly as their aircraft disintegrated in a ball of fire." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3a0f28af83c4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "With 60 seconds to decide whether the dot approaching at a rapid speed from 23,000ft was a friendly bomber returning from a mission over Baghdad or an incoming Iraqi missile, an American Patriot anti-aircraft battery opened fire." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/40aec4bcd0f3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The ground engineering check on ZG710's encrypted Mode 4 IFF was completed satisfactorily pre-engine start, and an RAF Regiment Rapier Missile unit that regularly checked the IFF of departing aircraft did not report the aircraft or log a fault." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49ca1ef1dea9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2299] However, the fundamental flaw which played a key part in the destruction of the Tornado was that its \"identification friend-or-foe\" (IFF) system which was supposed to send coded signals to anti-aircraft batteries had failed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49e1c89b1fd7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2299] After more than a year of investigation by the RAF and the US Army, it was revealed that several factors led to the disastrous 'friendly-fire' incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5454c9a7c69e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to a 2019 Center for Naval Analyses report, the Patriot recommended that the operator fire missiles in response to what it had identified as an enemy projectile." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ffb45d07d83> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2300] Since Operation Desert Storm, the United States Department of Defense has invested over $3.0 billion to further improve and extend Patriot ground equipment performance." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6f8f4cba4406> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tornado crew shot down after friend or foe system failed" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/714625858a4d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText " Investigation Finds U.S. Missiles Downed Navy Jet" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2298" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/80a7c4a42458> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2294] The Patriot missile began development in the 1960s, when the U.S. Army sought a means to reliably shoot down enemy airplanes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/94ebd995592e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As a 2005 report by the Defense Science Board Task Force on the Patriot system’s performance observed, operating autonomously required U.S. forces to trust that the automated features of the system were functioning properly." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a5d13305d6ab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Another system that failed and that might have prevented the shootdown was the identification-as-friend-or-foe system, a safety measure designed to avoid such deadly mistakes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aa65d4fb2af5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2299] The split-second decision led to one of the tragedies of the Iraq war last year: the dot was an RAF Tornado GR4, flown by Flight Lieutenants Kevin Main and David Williams who died instantly as their aircraft disintegrated in a ball of fire." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab571639e11a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The aircraft was about 16 miles from the Patriot missile location on the Kuwaiti/Iraqi border — one minute's flying time — when it received a direct hit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aeb52e662497> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However, the fundamental flaw which played a key part in the destruction of the Tornado was that its \"identification friend-or-foe\" (IFF) system which was supposed to send coded signals to anti-aircraft batteries had failed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b56d80efbb34> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Understanding the errors introduced by military AI applications" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bfc6ccf453f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "What the Patriot missile system had identified as an incoming missile, was in fact a UK Tornado fighter jet, and when the Patriot struck the aircraft, it killed two crew on board instantly." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2294" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c55f3b91e98d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2300] Last week's report by UK defence minister Ivor Caplin on the Tornado incident fingered a 'system error' as the cause, linked to failure of the aircraft's 'identification friend or foe' (IFF) system against a backdrop of of 'inexperienced US troops, heavily reliant on technology to make decisions, but lacking crucial equipment which could have helped them identify the Tornado as a friendly aircraft'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce3df9c7a595> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2300] Last week's report by UK defence minister Ivor Caplin on the Tornado incident fingered a 'system error' as the cause, linked to failure of the aircraft's 'identification friend or foe' (IFF) system against a backdrop of of 'inexperienced US troops, heavily reliant on technology to make decisions, but lacking crucial equipment which could have helped them identify the Tornado as a friendly aircraft'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2300" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cf961cd01be8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2296] Akiko Ohata White, the widow of Lt. Nathan White, said in papers filed in federal court in Boston that a Raytheon Patriot Missile system used by the U.S. Army shot down the plane in April 2003 after erroneously identifying it as an enemy missile." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2296" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d138b493343d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Woman Sues Raytheon Over Iraq Friendly Fire Death" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2296" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e91734b6965b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2299] With 60 seconds to decide whether the dot approaching at a rapid speed from 23,000ft was a friendly bomber returning from a mission over Baghdad or an incoming Iraqi missile, an American Patriot anti-aircraft battery opened fire." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2299" .

